   combination capability},
Journal = {TECHNOLOGY ANALYSIS \& STRATEGIC MANAGEMENT},
Year = {2025},
Volume = {37},
Number = {13},
Pages = {4316-4330},
Month = {DEC 5},
Abstract = {Although the digital innovation ecosystem provides opportunities to
   access diversified knowledge for knowledge creation in a digital
   context, it is still difficult to achieve the desired results due to the
   challenges of knowledge hiding and redundancy. This study adopts the
   knowledge-based view to investigate the relationship between knowledge
   compatibility and knowledge creation with the moderation of strategic
   compatibility and knowledge combination capability in the digital
   context. The results indicate that there is an inverted U-shaped
   relationship between knowledge compatibility and knowledge creation.
   Also, strategic compatibility and knowledge combination capability
   significantly moderate the inverted U-shaped relationship. Specifically,
   higher strategic compatibility and knowledge combination capability both
   reinforce the steeper curvilinear relationship. This study is a step
   forward in understanding the distinctive mechanism of how knowledge
   compatibility affects knowledge creation and extends the knowledge-based
   view in the digital innovation ecosystem.},
