Year = {2023},
Volume = {48},
Number = {2, SI},
Pages = {469-475},
Month = {APR},
Abstract = {This article introduces eleven research articles that connect concepts
   of technological relatedness and diffusion with the transformation of
   industrial and innovation systems. These studies focus on the role of
   knowledge spillovers, regional variations in innovation and performance,
   and the evolution of new technologies, such as green and digital
   technologies. Regional capabilities and ability to diversify are key in
   accelerating the transformation process of existing industries Taken all
   together, these studies suggest that industrial transformation hinge on
   firms capability to absorb domestic or foreign knowledge, regions
   capabilities, development trajectories, and their ability to network. In
   particular, regions capacity to diversify and leverage existing related
   knowledge are key in accelerating the green and digital transformation
   process of existing industries.},
